Z||000000||ChadMan||02-28-2000||09:36 AM||||You can find .wav audio files on the Net of everything from comedy bits to animal noises to Fiero engines.<P>Does anybody know how to make a .wav file?  If I take a tape recorder and a good microphone to the Nationals and come back with a tape of Northstars, 3800's, etc., is there a fairly easy way to post these on a Web site?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||overlord||02-28-2000||05:01 PM||||yup..this is easy..<P>just take your tape player and feed the output to the input on your soundcard.<P>and use a program like goldwave <A HREF="http://www.goldwave.com" TARGET=_blank>www.goldwave.com</A>  to record the wav.<P>here is a wav i did of my fiero (with the old engine..)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/downs/2634/mycar.wav" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/downs/2634/mycar.wav</A> <P>||||reg||1
